<title>SOUTH AFRICA: NBS, Boland to change name.</title>
<headline>NBS, Boland to change name.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>NBS Holdings and Boland Bank Holdings announced on Tuesday that their merged operations would be named NBS Boland Ltd with effect from early April this year.</p>
<p>The two banks merged in December last year, resulting in the creation of South Africa's fifth largest bank with total assets of about 26.5 billion rand.</p>
<p>Boland chief executive officer Michiel le Roux said all NBS and Boland divisions would continue to operate as they do now, while centralised funtions would be performed at the group's head office in Durban.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
